<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Fabric Guide</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Pants Fabric Guide | Choosing the Right Material for Your Style</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Cotton twill is a durable woven fabric with a diagonal rib pattern, making it the standard choice for chinos and casual trousers. With a GSM range of 240-320, cotton twill offers breathability, comfort, and excellent dye absorption. This fabric takes color well and maintains shape through regular wear, making it ideal for everyday pants that need to look professional while remaining comfortable.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Stretch cotton incorporates elastane for enhanced comfort and shape retention. With a 220-280 GSM range, this fabric provides the classic look of cotton with added flexibility. The stretch content typically ranges from 2-5%, allowing the pants to move with the wearer while returning to their original shape. This makes stretch cotton perfect for slim chinos and modern fits that require mobility without sacrificing appearance.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Linen blend fabrics combine natural linen with cotton or synthetic fibers for improved durability while maintaining the lightweight, breathable properties of pure linen. With a 180-240 GSM range, linen blend trousers are perfect for summer wear, offering superior cooling and casual elegance. The natural wrinkling characteristic of linen adds to its relaxed aesthetic, though the blend content reduces excessive wrinkling compared to pure linen.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Wool blend fabrics are premium materials for dress trousers and formal wear. With a 280-360 GSM range, wool-polyester blends offer excellent drape, wrinkle resistance, and temperature regulation. These fabrics provide the polished appearance required for suits and business attire while being more practical than pure wool in terms of care and maintenance. Our <a href="/denim-manufacturer" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:underline;">denim manufacturer</a> also produces specialized denim trousers for casual markets.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Polyester blend fabrics (180-260 GSM) are durable, wrinkle-resistant, and easy-care options for joggers, casual trousers, and work pants. Polyester-cotton blends combine natural comfort with synthetic durability, creating fabrics that resist fading, shrinking, and pilling. These are popular choices for uniform applications and everyday casual wear where practicality is a priority.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Denim (cotton, 280-400 GSM) is a classic cotton twill fabric used for jeans and casual trousers. Available in various weights, washes, and finishes, denim is rugged and versatile for casual wear. Heavyweight denim (14oz+) provides durability for work applications, while lighter weights (10-12oz) offer comfort for everyday jeans. Our <a href="/workwear-manufacturer" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:underline;">workwear manufacturer</a> specializes in heavy-duty denim for industrial applications.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Tencel and lyocell fabrics (200-260 GSM) are sustainable options for casual trousers, offering a silky feel and excellent drape. These cellulosic fibers are produced from wood pulp through environmentally responsible processes. Tencel fabrics are moisture-wicking, breathable, and resistant to wrinkles, making them premium choices for eco-conscious brands seeking sustainable alternatives to traditional fabrics.
    </p>
    
