<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Quality Control</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Pants Quality Standards | What to Inspect Before Shipping</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      AQL inspection standards are fundamental to pants manufacturing quality control. SDF Clothing follows AQL 2.5 for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, ensuring that trousers and pants meet rigorous quality benchmarks before shipment. This statistical sampling method allows us to inspect a representative sample from each production lot, identifying defects that would affect customer satisfaction.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Inline inspection during pants production focuses on critical construction points. Our quality team monitors waistband attachment, fly construction, pocket installation, and hem finishing at multiple stages. This real-time quality control catches issues like uneven waistbands, misaligned pockets, or improper hem depths before garments progress to completion, reducing rework and ensuring consistency.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Final inspection for pants evaluates seam strength, zipper functionality, button security, and overall garment symmetry. We verify that front and back rises match, side seams are equal length, and leg openings are consistent within size specifications. Our <a href="/quality-inspection-service" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:underline;">quality inspection service</a> provides comprehensive reports documenting all measurements and visual assessments.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Common defects in pants manufacturing include uneven waistlines, twisted legs, puckered seams, and loose threads. Fit-specific defects include tight thighs in slim fit pants or excessive bagginess in dress pants. Our inspection protocol includes checks for these recurring issues, with specific tolerance levels for each garment type and fit category.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Understanding inspection reports requires knowledge of defect severity and acceptance thresholds. Major defects such as holes, stains, or broken zippers result in automatic rejection, while minor issues like slight thread variations may be acceptable within AQL limits. Our reports clearly document findings with severity classifications and photographic evidence for transparency.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Performance testing for pants includes wash testing for shrinkage and color fastness, durability testing for seam strength under stress, and functionality testing for closures and fasteners. These tests ensure that pants will maintain their fit, appearance, and functionality through normal use and laundering cycles. We conduct these tests on sample garments from each production run.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

